AB  - While mobile computing is ubiquitous, it fails to capture complex thoughts on the go, leading to frustrating idea loss. This work reframes this problem as a need for cognitive empowerment, proposing wearable AI assistants as "cognitive partners" that utilise Large Language Models (LLMs) and Optical See-Through Head-Mounted Displays (OHMDs). We identify the core challenge as the high metacognitive demands of mobile human-AI collaboration under mobile constraints. Our primary contribution is the deconstruction of this challenge into fundamental conflicts between Platform and Cognitive Challenges. We then leverage a three-layer frame-work – Perception → Interaction → Cognition – to structure the problem space and define a research agenda.
