AB  - This paper presents a Virtual Reality (VR) Classroom framework designed to enhance immersive learning experiences for students using Artificial Intelligence. The framework integrates 3D environments, speech-based interaction, and retrieval-augmented generation to support both traditional and special-needs education. Student input is captured via the headset’s microphone, transcribed by Whisper speech-to-text, and processed to generate curriculum-aligned responses. These are delivered as written text and natural speech using the Piper text-to-speech model with avatar lip synchronization, creating a dualchannel learning experience. A prototype demonstrates improved engagement, accessibility, and comprehension, while challenges such as scalability, hardware requirements, and integration are discussed.
