AB  - With the widespread application of virtual reality (VR) technology in the fields of entertainment and education, the immersion experienced by users in VR movies and TV shows has become a key factor affecting their acceptance and satisfaction. However, there are still significant shortcomings in terms of image rendering speed in current VR movies and TV shows. This article introduces an algorithm optimization framework based on Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN). Firstly, this article uses CNN algorithm to optimize the image rendering process. Next, use Dynamic Resolution Adjustment (DRS) technology to improve rendering speed and maintain frame rate stability; Then, combining high dynamic range (HDR) rendering and temporal anti aliasing (TAA) technology to enhance the color expression and visual smoothness of the image; Finally, optimize the sensor data processing flow and data transmission protocol. Through experimental evaluation in VR scenes of different complexities, the results showed that the optimized system improved rendering speed by an average of about 58.3%, reduced interaction latency by about 33.3%, and improved image quality indicators PSNR and SSIM by about 26.2% and 9%, respectively. In the above data conclusions, CNN based optimization methods have shown significant advantages in improving VR film and television performance and user experience, providing strong support for the future development of VR film and television technology.
ER  - 

