AB  - Medicinal plants are essential for healthcare and its related applications. Learning about them is important to gain valuable knowledge about botany, plant life cycles, and natural remedies. Engaging and accessible methods of learning increase the effectiveness of plant learning methodologies. This work presents an augmented reality framework for immersive medicinal plant learning which combines three-dimensional spatial visualizations with educational insights and information. The proposed system integrates a virtual garden with an AI-powered chatbot for interactive learning. The virtual 3D models of the medicinal plants can be placed in real world environments using AR, the comprehensive information about the plant can be accessed and AI chatbot responds to natural language queries about plant properties, cultivation and medicinal applications. The system is evaluated using learning gain, user engagement and usability assessments. The results demonstrate a positive user experience, high interaction and effective learning. These results show that the proposed system successfully uses AR and AI technologies for an accessible and engaging learning experience of medicinal plant education. It supports botanical learning and contributes to quality health education aligned with sustainable development goals.
