AB  - The digital preservation of cultural heritage requires effective coordination between historical continuity and contemporary public participation. Taking the Historic Centre of Macau as the research object, this study develops an AIGC-based framework for digital reconstruction and interactive cultural communication. The framework combines Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) with Virtual Reality (VR) technologies to achieve historical pattern generation and immersive scene presentation. Through the integration of cultural data resources and interactive media technologies, the system enables the transformation of historical archives into dynamic community art experiences. A total of 120 participants were involved in the experimental evaluation of the platform. The results indicate that the proposed interactive system increases user engagement by 34.5% and improves cultural identity perception by 28.2% compared with conventional digital archive platforms. In addition, the generated historical patterns achieved a structural similarity index (SSIM) above 0.85, demonstrating high consistency in visual reconstruction. The study provides a digital approach for cultural memory preservation and interactive heritage communication in urban historical communities.
