AB  - As the core equipment for power transmission and voltage transformation in electrical power systems, power transformers require withstand voltage experiment, which are a key technical means for detecting insulation reliability and preventing operational failures. Traditional training for withstand voltage experiment relies on theoretical instruction from textbooks and a “master-apprentice” model for practical skill transfer. This approach results in suboptimal training outcomes due to limited hands-on opportunities and poses significant safety risks when inexperienced personnel directly operate real equipment. To address the pain points of traditional training methods—poor effectiveness, high costs, and insufficient safety—this paper proposes a virtual reality (VR)-based 3D simulation training method for power transformer withstand voltage experiment. By deeply integrating VR technology with operational training for withstand voltage experiment, this method effectively resolves the challenges of “high cost, high consumption, and high risk” faced by current training centers. Compared to traditional training models, the constructed system demonstrates significant improvements in key metrics such as trainee satisfaction and training effectiveness.
ER  - 

