AB  - How to holistically present ancient poetry remains a key challenge in cultural digitalization, as traditional teaching methods often overlook emotional engagement and result in a monotonous learning experience. Reconstructing poetic scenes via Virtual Reality (VR) is a promising solution; yet, existing VR-based systems are plagued by inefficient scene construction and simplistic interaction modalities. To address these limitations, this study makes three key contributions: first, designing Poetry-GenScene—an AI Agent framework powered by large language models (LLMs) that understands user intentions, formulates task plans, and proactively deploys tools for poetry appreciation instruction and VR scene generation; second, developing an immersive VR experiential learning system for classical Chinese poetry, integrated with multimodal interaction (speech and gesture), which enables natural human–computer communication in VR environments; third, proposing an automatic real-time VR scene generation mechanism that converts poetic textual features into scene parameters and generates corresponding immersive scenes within seconds. Distinguished from previous work that relies on manual pre-construction of VR scenes or single-modal interaction, the proposed system achieves high automation and natural interaction, while exhibiting enhanced generalizability to the vast corpus of ancient poetry. Experimental results demonstrate that the system can generate VR scenes corresponding to the target poems in real time (within seconds), thereby providing users with immersive poetic experiences. This system significantly improves users’ poetry comprehension and memory, with excellent usability and interaction experience
ER  - 

