AB  - This paper presents an AR-based auxiliary processing system for aerospace cable assembly that overcomes critical limitations of manual interpretation. The framework integrates: (1) hierarchical Extensible Markup Language (XML) modeling converting cable schematics into real-time Augmented Reality (AR) visualizations; (2) a domain-specific knowledge base with optimized 3D connector models and processing rules; and (3) a multi-modal interface combining offline speech recognition (2.35% WER), gesture control (96.8% F1-score), and adaptive Optical Character Recognition(OCR) (98.7% character accuracy). Validated on production cables, the system achieved zero contact-mapping errors (100% accuracy) and reduced interpretation time by 87% compared to manual methods. Electrical tests confirmed full compliance with Q/W1037A-2015 standards (0.48±0.22Ω conduction resistance; 502–850 MΩ insulation resistance). Notably, novice operator error rates dropped from 12.7% to 0.9% with AR guidance. Spatial registration precision (1.24±0.31 mm) met aerospace tolerances, while SPARQL-based rule retrieval achieved 0.97 F1-score. This work establishes a robust AR-IoT framework for mission-critical manufacturing, demonstrating significant gains in quality, efficiency, and skill accessibility.
